  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental lines from the 2024 Total Governmental Funds column (p4); roll-forward 163,066 + 214,914 - 316,227 + 10,000 - 10,000 = 61,753 (ending fund balance = cash 76,381 + investments 50,144 + due from other governments 2,815 - bank overdraft 67,587, p3). Business-type from the proprietary statement (p6), which carries capital assets and depreciation, so measure net position; no single total printed, operating + nonoperating added. Proprietary cash flow statement (pp7-8) not recorded (proprietary is for GAAP reports). Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position 2024 Total column (p1), since it includes capital assets and debt. Detail: budgetary comparison schedules for every fund (pp9-16; Original and Final budget column). The Keno Fund schedule prints no total revenue or total expenditure line, so it has no detail_totals entry. Water/Sewer budget schedules are on the budgetary (cash) basis: debt service is principal and interest combined and capital outlay is shown instead of depreciation. Read pages 1-16 of 16"
}
